-- title:
--   SL₂(ℤ)-invariance of E₄³/Δ
-- statement:
--   For every $\gamma$ in the special linear group $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ (Mathlib's `Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℤ`) and every point $\tau$ of the upper half-plane $\mathfrak{H}$, the complex number $E_4(\gamma\cdot\tau)^3/\Delta(\gamma\cdot\tau)$ equals $E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$. Here $E_4$ is Mathlib's normalised weight-$4$ Eisenstein series `ModularForm.E₄` for the full modular group, $\Delta$ is the modular discriminant `ModularForm.discriminant`, $\gamma\cdot\tau$ is the usual action of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ on $\mathfrak{H}$ by fractional linear transformations, and the cube and the quotient are taken in $\mathbb{C}$. No non-vanishing hypothesis on $\Delta$ enters: with Lean's convention $x/0 = 0$ the asserted identity holds as stated, so this is exactly the invariance of the function $\tau \mapsto E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$ on $\mathfrak{H}$ under the full modular group, with no claim that the common value is finite or that it computes the $j$-invariant up to a constant.
--
--   This is the $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$-invariance of the level-one modular function $E_4^3/\Delta$, i.e. of the modular invariant $j$ up to normalisation. It is used in the treatment of the modular curve: stabiliser and ramification computations for complex points, membership statements for algebras generated by $j$ and $q$, and the Fricke involution on $\Gamma_0$-invariant expansions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_E4_cube_div_discriminant_smul.lean

import Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.EisensteinSeries.Basic
import Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.Discriminant

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.E4_cube_div_discriminant_smul (γ : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℤ) (τ : UpperHalfPlane) : ModularForm.E₄ (γ • τ) ^ 3 / ModularForm.discriminant (γ • τ) = ModularForm.E₄ τ ^ 3 / ModularForm.discriminant τ := by sorry
